@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "provisioning.security"

Feature: Koroneiki To Provisioning License API Okta Authentication
	Testing Okta Authentication permission for users

Setup:
	* I get all test passwords and admin emails
	* I generate several static variables for Provisioning
	* I generate a provisioning company name
	* I generate a provisioning project name
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | pro.okta1                       |
	| Email Address | pro.okta1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | PRO                             |
	| Last Name     | Okta1                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | pro.okta2                       |
	| Email Address | pro.okta2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | PRO                             |
	| Last Name     | Okta2                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | pro.okta3                      |
	| Email Address | pro.okta3@lrpartner.com.broken |
	| First Name    | PRO                            |
	| Last Name     | Okta3                          |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | pro.okta4                       |
	| Email Address | pro.okta4@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | PRO                             |
	| Last Name     | Okta4                           |

Teardown:
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the first default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Misper - ${staticCompanyName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the second default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Perpar - ${staticCompanyName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the third default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Kormis - ${staticCompanyName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the third default user ID variable
	* I tear down the product consumption list on koroneiki made by the account "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" for the following products
	| DXP Production    |
	| Portal Production |
	* I tear down the product consumption list on koroneiki made by the account "Kormis - ${staticProjectName}" for the following products
	| DXP Production    |
	| Portal Production |
	* I tear down the product consumptions on koroneiki made by the account "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" for the following products
	| DXP Production    |
	| Portal Production |
	* I tear down the product consumptions on koroneiki made by the account "Kormis - ${staticProjectName}" for the following products
	| DXP Production    |
	| Portal Production |
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I tear down the product consumption list on koroneiki made by the account "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" for the following products
	| DXP Production    |
	| Portal Production |
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Kormis - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I tear down the product consumption list on koroneiki made by the account "Kormis - ${staticProjectName}" for the following products
	| DXP Production    |
	| Portal Production |
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes
	| MISPERPERMIS |
	| MISKORKORMIS |
	| MISPER       |
	| PERPAR       |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Permis - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Misper - ${staticCompanyName} |
	| Perpar - ${staticCompanyName} |
	| Kormis - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| MISPERPERMIS |
	| MISKORKORMIS |
	| MISPER       |
	| PERPAR       |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from web.liferay.com
	| pro.okta1@lrcustomer.com.broken   |
	| pro.okta2@lrcustomer.com.broken   |
	| pro.okta3@lrpartner.com.broken    |
	| pro.okta4@lrcustomer.com.broken   |
	| okta.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| pro.okta1@lrcustomer.com.broken   |
	| pro.okta2@lrcustomer.com.broken   |
	| pro.okta3@lrpartner.com.broken    |
	| pro.okta4@lrcustomer.com.broken   |
	| okta.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from koroneiki
	| pro.okta1@lrcustomer.com.broken   |
	| pro.okta2@lrcustomer.com.broken   |
	| pro.okta3@lrpartner.com.broken    |
	| pro.okta4@lrcustomer.com.broken   |
	| okta.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| pro.okta1@lrcustomer.com.broken   |
	| pro.okta2@lrcustomer.com.broken   |
	| pro.okta3@lrpartner.com.broken    |
	| pro.okta4@lrcustomer.com.broken   |
	| okta.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from okta
	| pro.okta1@lrcustomer.com.broken   |
	| pro.okta2@lrcustomer.com.broken   |
	| pro.okta3@lrpartner.com.broken    |
	| pro.okta4@lrcustomer.com.broken   |
	| okta.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	* I teardown the tickets with the following keywords from zendesk.liferay.com
	| New Subscription(s) for Permis - ${staticProjectName} |
	| New Subscription(s) for Misper - ${staticCompanyName} |
	| New Subscription(s) for Perpar - ${staticCompanyName} |
	| New Subscription(s) for Kormis - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| pro.okta1@lrcustomer.com.broken   |
	| pro.okta2@lrcustomer.com.broken   |
	| pro.okta3@lrpartner.com.broken    |
	| pro.okta4@lrcustomer.com.broken   |
	| okta.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com if still present
	| Permis - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Misper - ${staticCompanyName} |
	| Perpar - ${staticCompanyName} |
	| Kormis - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId1}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId2}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId3}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: View license with Provisioning API and okta authentication using a valid user
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	Testing the ability to view a license form options with Provisioning API and okta authentication

	Given I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Misper - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | pro.okta1@lrcustomer.com.broken            |
	| Contact First Name                     | PRO                                        |
	| Contact Last Name                      | Okta1                                      |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                 |
	| Owner Email Address                    | pro.okta1@lrcustomer.com.broken            |
	| Owner First Name                       | PRO                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Okta1                                      |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | Liferay Digital Enterprise - Prod Sizing 4 |
	| Project Name                           | Permis - ${staticProjectName}              |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                        |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticProvisioningAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticProvisioningAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the license index page
	And I click on the generate license button on the license index
	And I populate the generate license form with the following values
	| Account | Select Entity | Permis - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Product | Select        | DXP Production                | |
	| Version | Select        | 7.2                           | |
	| Type    | Select        | DXP Production                | |
	And I click on the choose button for the product purchase in position "1" on the license form
	And I populate the generate license form with the following values
	| Host Name     | Input    | localhost         | |
	| IP Addresses  | Textarea | 123.45.67.89      | |
	| MAC Addresses | Textarea | 0A-1B-2C-3D-4E-5F | |
	And I click on the generate button on the license form
	Then I should be able to view the following license values on the license page
	| Header  | Permis - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Product | DXP Production                | |
	When I log into the dev domain as "pro.okta1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "${staticOktaUserPassword}"
	And I obtain the okta session ID value from the dev domain page
	Then I should be able to view the license on the account "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" with the name "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" using okta session id
	And I should be able to view the following generate license form options for the account "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" with the product group "DXP" using okta session id
	| Label | 7.0 | | |
	| Label | 7.1 | | |
	| Label | 7.2 | | |
	| Label | 7.3 | | |
	| Label | 7.4 | | |

Scenario: View FLS partner license with Provisioning API and okta authentication using a valid user
	Testing the ability to view FLS partner license form options with Provisioning API and a valid okta Session ID

	Given I publish a partner account RabbitMQ message with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Perpar - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ijklmnop1234567890                         |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Professional Services (Technical/Web/IT)   |
	| Owner Email Address                    | pro.okta3@lrpartner.com.broken             |
	| Owner First Name                       | PRO                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Okta3                                      |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Name                           | Service Partnership                        |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | 000000g1h2cid4j5k6l7m                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Partner"
	And I publish a project RabbitMQ message with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Misper - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | pro.okta1@lrcustomer.com.broken            |
	| Contact First Name                     | PRO                                        |
	| Contact Last Name                      | Okta1                                      |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                 |
	| Owner Email Address                    | pro.okta1@lrcustomer.com.broken            |
	| Owner First Name                       | PRO                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Okta1                                      |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Partner Dossiera Key                   | ijklmnop1234567890                         |
	| Partner Name                           | Perpar - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Partner Support Level                  | Platinum                                   |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | Liferay Digital Enterprise - Prod Sizing 4 |
	| Project Name                           | Permis - ${staticProjectName}              |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                        |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "pro.okta3@lrpartner.com.broken" on the account "Perpar - ${staticCompanyName}" to the following roles
	| Partner Member |
	When I log into the dev domain as "pro.okta3@lrpartner.com.broken" with password "${staticOktaUserPassword}"
	And I obtain the okta session ID value from the dev domain page
	And I create an assigned team nested field for a team with the name "Perpar - ${staticCompanyName}" assigned to the account "Permis - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I assign the team with the name "Perpar - ${staticCompanyName}" on the account "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Partner |
	And I assign the team with the name "Perpar - ${staticCompanyName}" on the account "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| First Line Support |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Partner"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Partner"
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticProvisioningAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticProvisioningAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the license index page
	And I click on the generate license button on the license index
	And I populate the generate license form with the following values
	| Account | Select Entity | Permis - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Product | Select        | DXP Production                | |
	| Version | Select        | 7.2                           | |
	| Type    | Select        | DXP Production                | |
	And I click on the choose button for the product purchase in position "1" on the license form
	And I populate the generate license form with the following values
	| Host Name     | Input    | localhost         | |
	| IP Addresses  | Textarea | 123.45.67.89      | |
	| MAC Addresses | Textarea | 0A-1B-2C-3D-4E-5F | |
	And I click on the generate button on the license form
	Then I should be able to view the following license values on the license page
	| Header  | Permis - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Product | DXP Production                | |
	When I log into the dev domain as "pro.okta3@lrpartner.com.broken" with password "${staticOktaUserPassword}"
	And I obtain the okta session ID value from the dev domain page
	Then I should be able to view the license on the account "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" with the name "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" using okta session id 
	And I should be able to view the following generate license form options for the account "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" with the product group "DXP" using okta session id
	| Label | 7.1 | | |
	| Label | 7.2 | | |
	| Label | 7.3 | | |
	| Label | 7.4 | | |

Scenario: View license attempt with Provisioning API and okta authentication using a non permissioned user
	Testing the attempt to view a license form options with a invalid okta Session Id

	Given I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Misper - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | pro.okta2@lrcustomer.com.broken            |
	| Contact First Name                     | PRO                                        |
	| Contact Last Name                      | Okta1                                      |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                 |
	| Owner Email Address                    | pro.okta2@lrcustomer.com.broken            |
	| Owner First Name                       | PRO                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Okta2                                      |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | Liferay Digital Enterprise - Prod Sizing 4 |
	| Project Name                           | Permis - ${staticProjectName}              |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                        |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticProvisioningAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticProvisioningAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the license index page
	And I click on the generate license button on the license index
	And I populate the generate license form with the following values
	| Account | Select Entity | Permis - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Product | Select        | DXP Production                | |
	| Version | Select        | 7.2                           | |
	| Type    | Select        | DXP Production                | |
	And I click on the choose button for the product purchase in position "1" on the license form
	And I populate the generate license form with the following values
	| Host Name     | Input    | localhost         | |
	| IP Addresses  | Textarea | 123.45.67.89      | |
	| MAC Addresses | Textarea | 0A-1B-2C-3D-4E-5F | |
	And I click on the generate button on the license form
	Then I should be able to view the following license values on the license page
	| Header  | Permis - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Product | DXP Production                | |
	When I log into the dev domain as "pro.okta1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "${staticOktaUserPassword}"
	And I obtain the okta session ID value from the dev domain page
	Then I should not be able to view the license on the account "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" with the name "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" using okta session id
	And I should be able to view a license search error when searching for a license with the name "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" on the account "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" using okta session id

Scenario: Generate license with Provisioning API and okta authentication using a Liferay Sales user
	Testing the attempt to generate a license with Provisioning API and a valid okta Session ID using a Liferay Sales user

	Given I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Misper - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | pro.okta1@lrcustomer.com.broken            |
	| Contact First Name                     | PRO                                        |
	| Contact Last Name                      | Okta1                                      |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                 |
	| Owner Email Address                    | pro.okta2@lrcustomer.com.broken            |
	| Owner First Name                       | PRO                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Okta2                                      |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | Liferay Digital Enterprise - Prod Sizing 4 |
	| Project Name                           | Permis - ${staticProjectName}              |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                        |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I generate the product purchase key value for the product purchase made by "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" for "DXP Production"
	When I log into the dev domain as "pro.okta2@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "${staticOktaUserPassword}"
	And I obtain the okta session ID value from the dev domain page
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticProvisioningAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticProvisioningAdminPassword}"
	And I create a license with the following parameters on the account "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" and product purchase "DXP Production" using okta session id with the following values
	| Active                     | true                          |
	| Expiration Date            | ${staticEndDate}              |
	| License Entry Type         | production                    |
	| Max Cluster Nodes          | 0                             |
	| Name                       | Permis - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Product Version            | 7.4                           |
	| Start Date                 | ${staticStartDate}            |
	And I go to the license index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Permis"
	And I click on the account with the name "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	When I click on the "Licenses" tab
	Then I should be able to view the license with the keyword "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" and the following values on the account details page
	| Name          | Permis - ${staticProjectName}  |
	| Description   | Permis - ${staticProjectName}  |
	| Product       | DXP Production                 |
	| Type          | Production                     |
	| Details       | Host Name: localhost           |
	| Details       | IP Address: 123.45.67.89       |
	| Details       | MAC Address: 0A-1B-2C-3D-4E-5F |
	| Status        | ACTIVE                         |
	| Complimentary | false                          |
	When I click on the "History" tab
	Then the history entry with the keyword "PRO Okta2 > Added License Key" with the field value "sizing" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | PRO Okta2 > Added License Key |
